# Git: SSH + auto commit / merge

- Use SSH remotes only (`git@github.com:...`). Never switch origin back to HTTPS.
- Rely on `core.sshCommand` / Git's bundled SSH (`C:/Program Files/Git/usr/bin/ssh.exe`).
- After finishing a task with file changes: `git add`, commit with a clear message, `git pull --no-rebase` (merge remote), then `git push` over SSH.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys, tokens).
- If the stop/afterFileEdit auto-git hook already committed and pushed, do not create a duplicate empty commit.
